# Build context is the repo root. Everything the two Dockerfiles need is COPYed
# explicitly, so this mostly keeps heavy, host-specific junk out of the context
# transfer — with one exception that matters for correctness:
#
# `COPY apps/api apps/api` would otherwise bake the developer's own
# apps/api/.env into the production image. env.ts fills in any variable the
# stack file did NOT set from that file, so a local Stripe key or build-host
# credential would silently become production config. The `**/` prefix is
# required — a bare `.env` pattern matches only the context root. (The image
# also sets SKIP_DOTENV, so this is the first of two locks on the same door.)
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local

node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
.git
.tmp
logs
References
infra/seed
apps/desktop/src-tauri
**/*.log
